Surrey County Council&#039;s Transport Model is used to assist with funding bids, scheme development, option testing, information for consultations, business cases, asset management maintenance options, environmental assessments, and partner authority Local 
Plan development, including the provision of evidence for consultations and examinations. 

Within Surrey County Council, the model is used to support work undertaken by other teams, in particular Transport Policy, Asset Management and the Design Team .

The current County Transport Model requires a complete renewal if it is continued to be used as its current software platform is no longer suitable for Surrey&#039;s needs and because the base model is pre-pandemic and needs to reflect post-pandemic travel patterns.

The objectives of the procurement are: 
• Move the model to a new software platform;
• Capture up-to-date travel pattern data;
• Secure a new model build that is fit for purpose.

The contribution to the Community vision for Surrey in 2030 that this project will make are:
• Journeys across the county are easier, more predictable and safer;
• Everyone has a place they can call home with appropriate housing for all;
• Well-connected communities with effective infrastructure that grow sustainably

This opportunity is a mini-competition under lot 8f of the ESPO Framework Agreement reference 664-21 &#039;Consultancy Services&#039; via the Proactis Supplier Network. As your organisation is a contractor under the above framework, we would be interested in receiving a response from your organisation with regard to this opportunity. Please note that this opportunity is only open to contractors on the ESPO 664-21 framework. 
      
      Surrey County Council is seeking to construct and operate a new materials recovery facility (MRF) of up to 100,000 tonnes per annum (tpa) capacity, to receive and sort dry mixed recycling (DMR) from local authority collected waste (LACW).    
      
      The MRF would be located at Land adjacent to Trumps Farm, Kitsmead Lane, Longcross, KT16 0EF. 
      
      Surrey County Council is seeking a qualified and experienced Consultant to develop the scope of the project and prepare the required planning submission, incorporating the application, drawings and all necessary assessments.  
      
      The Consultant will be responsible for:  
      1. Developing an optimal scheme and masterplanning the site;  
      2. Identifying all necessary assessments and documents to comprise the planning application, and preparing them;  
      3. Preparing all necessary plans and drawings (other than architectural);  
      4. Undertaking pre-application consultation;  
      5. Submitting any resultant application;  
      6. Providing post-submission support, as required.  
      
      SCC intends to run the commission in four phases:  
      1. Developing the Project;  
      2. Preparing the Planning Application;  
      3. Draft of Planning Application;  
      4. Submission of Planning Application and Post-Submission Support.  
      
      Each phase of work will be awarded separately and there is no guarantee that Surrey County Council will progress to the next phase.
